  "description": "Harness-seeded two-VM guest-static-IP V2 template. Two standalone client VMs on the SAME dedicated Internal lab switch, each with a single NIC bound by networkId and holding its OWN distinct static IP (10.81.0.21/24 and 10.81.0.22/24). Both reference the REAL prepared Windows Server base image (guest-configurable via its bootstrap profile), so the plan requires guest work and can only start once the local bootstrap credential slot is filled. Proves per-adapter MAC binding: EACH VM must end up holding its own templated IP, without the router/Default-Switch egress complication. Safe to delete.",
